35,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,The room usage is wildly uneven. One room uses four times more than another.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Mio,,The template trial was a nightmare. Keying in every invoice took hours.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,The payment log shows three late payments. People are anxious about the amounts.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,The winter bill is nearly triple the summer bill. The electrician quote is steep.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Minato,,The cooler notice stayed up all summer. People were just suffering to avoid conflict.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Victoria, if we meter the rooms, the upfront cost is high, but it’s fair.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Benjamin, but who maintains the meters? I don’t want to be the one checking them.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Mio, the reconciliation template was too complex. We need something simpler.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Jonathan, the seasonal swing is too big for a flat rate. It feels unfair in winter.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Minato,,I think a fixed seasonal rate might work. It’s predictable.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,I’m leaning towards per-room metering. It’s the only way to be truly fair.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Mio,,I’m worried about the admin. Maybe a seasonal fixed rate is better?,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,I agree with Mio. The payment log shows people hate surprises. Predictability is key.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,I’m hesitant. The upfront cost for meters is high. But the seasonal rate risks a big year-end bill.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Minato,,I like the idea of a seasonal rate. It feels less like a fight.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I’ll vote for metering. It’s the most logical solution.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Mio,,I’ll vote for the seasonal rate. I can’t handle the admin of meters.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I’ll vote for the seasonal rate. It reduces the friction I saw in the logs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I’ll vote for the seasonal rate. The metering cost is too high for the benefit.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Minato,,I’ll vote for the seasonal rate. It feels peaceful.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
